      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "e85ed4449ea34c4658a7fed8961f9ca3b8ffbbe3",
            "subject": "LU-20995 compat: fail cleanly on kallsyms lookups with x86 IBT"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Jian Yu",
          "email": "yujian@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-24 04:48:42.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Jian Yu",
          "email": "yujian@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-24 04:52:45.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-20995 compat: call kallsyms functions via static_call",
        "message": "LU-20995 compat: call kallsyms functions via static_call\n\nOn x86 kernels with CONFIG_X86_KERNEL_IBT running on an IBT-enabled\nCPU, libcfs refuses to load with -EOPNOTSUPP: kallsyms_lookup_name(),\nalloc/free/apply_workqueue_attrs() and security_file_alloc/free()\nhave their ENDBR sealed because the kernel never takes their address,\nso calling them through a pointer would raise #CP.  Lustre can only\nbe used with ibt=off.\n\nA direct call or jmp does not need an ENDBR.  With IBT, define a\nstatic_call() in libcfs for each function that lustre_symbols_init()\nlooks up, and for kallsyms_lookup_name() itself, and point it at the\nkallsyms address with static_call_update().  The call sites are then\npatched into direct calls to the kernel function, so the ENDBR check\nis no longer needed for them.  Other kernels keep calling through a\nfunction pointer, behind the same CFS_DEFINE_SYMBOL(),\ncfs_symbol_call() and cfs_symbol_set() helpers.\n\ncfs_kallsyms_lookup_func() keeps its ENDBR check for callers outside\nlibcfs that call the result through a pointer.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity clientdistro=el10.2\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity clientdistro=el10.1\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity clientdistro=el9.8\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity clientdistro=el8.10\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity clientdistro=sles15sp7\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity clientdistro=ubuntu2404\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity clientdistro=ubuntu2604\n\nSigned-off-by: Jian Yu <yujian@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ifbe9bcb2ed7d84121de7db2eb5fc3cfff104b985\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
